<Layout title="Our Story | Manchester Select" description="The story behind Manchester Select, from Sarah’s diagnosis to a community rugby league charity raising money for The Christie.">
  <section class="policy"><div class="eyebrow">Manchester Select</div><h1>Our Story</h1><p class="lead">What started with a diagnosis became a reason to bring a community together.</p>
  <img src={raw+'event2.png'} alt="Manchester Select charity rugby event" style="margin:45px 0;border-radius:24px;max-height:620px;width:100%;object-fit:cover" />
  <h2>Sarah’s diagnosis</h2><p>Manchester Select began with a very personal reason to act. Sarah’s diagnosis changed the perspective of everyone around her. Chris and Nick wanted to turn that experience into something positive — something that could bring people together and raise money for The Christie.</p>
  <h2>The first event</h2><p>The idea was simple: use the sport they loved to create an event people would want to attend. Players, clubs, supporters and local businesses came together to make the first Manchester Select fixture possible. The day became more than a game; it became a shared statement that a community can do something meaningful when it pulls together.</p>
  <h2>Growing the idea</h2><p>The first event gave Manchester Select momentum. The September 2024 programme brought a charity match against Great Britain Police and a women’s fixture against Keighley Cougars, helping raise more than £85,000 and welcoming around 1,400 spectators across two events.</p>
  <h2>What comes next</h2><p>Manchester Select is now about building a lasting platform for sport, community and fundraising. Rugby league remains at the heart of the story, but the ambition is to create more events, more partnerships and more opportunities for people to get involved.</p>
  <a class="button button-dark" href="/#contact">Be part of the next chapter</a></section>
</Layout>
